  "status": "Refused",
  "actual_commencement_date": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal, by reason of loss of houses -although in despair- which complements with the original estate and integral to the character and appearance of the area, with no evidence to suggest cannot be refurbished would be harmful to the heritage and not promote sustainability; also the proposal, by reason of its position, size, design and external appearance would be an intrusive development, out of scale and character with the prevailing pattern of development and have a serious and adverse effect on the visual amenity of the locality and the wider Gunnersbury Park Conservation Area (Article 4), contrary to Local Plan policies SC7, CC1, CC2 and CC4 and London Plan Policy D4 and the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal would result in an intensification of the use of the site leading to an increase in noise and disturbance in the area, and no measures are proposed to mitigate the harm, would cause a serious and adverse effect on the amenity enjoyed by occupants of neighbouring properties and the character of the area, contrary to Local Plan Policies SC7 and CC2 and the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposal provides inadequate quality of accommodation; due to poor outlook and light levels and provision of five of the eight proposed flats with insufficient provision of private amenity space and so would be detrimental to the amenities enjoyed by prospective occupants of this development. The proposed development is therefore contrary to Local Plan policies SC5, CC2, and London Plan Policy D6, London Plan Housing SPG and the intent of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 4 - The proposal does not demonstrate that the 10% Be Lean carbon saving over part L is met. In addition domestic triple glazing with u-value around 1.0 is not proposed. The 50% carbon reduction target is not met and no calculation for the carbon offset payment to achieve net-zero carbon has been provided or confirmed. As a result the proposal does not meet the Council's sustainability standards contrary to Local Plan Policy EQ1 and London Plan Policy SI2 and the intent of the National Planning Policy Framework."
  ],
